    "comparison_component": {
      "branch": "jp",
      "slug": "component:collapsible-sidebar",
      "revision": 4,
      "source_sha256": "b0ae91dbf313be853ab0a8e130176b2dc6bd5a9543d1f97687fc4cf9432db55f"
    },
    "conclusion": "The current English and Japanese toggle descriptions specify a corner button. They explicitly distinguish the collapsible sidebar as hover-based rather than click-based. The toggle source has hover selectors for an already reachable sidebar, but no source authority requires a closed sidebar to expose an edge activation rail. Edge-hover-open from rest is non-normative; button/focus opening and hover after opening remain distinct observations."
  },
